{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry#def:l-jacobi-field","title":"def:l-jacobi-field","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry.md","line":199,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry.tex#def:l-jacobi-field","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry#lem:l-jacobi-equation]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry.tex","label":"def:l-jacobi-field","line":310,"source":"\\begin{definition}[${\\mathcal L}$-Jacobi field]\\label{def:l-jacobi-field}\n\\uses{lem:l-jacobi-equation}\n\nA field $Y(\\tau)$ along an ${\\mathcal L}$-geodesic is\ncalled an {\\em ${\\mathcal L}$-Jacobi field} if it satisfies the ${\\mathcal L}$-Jacobi\nequation, Equation~(\\ref{jaceqn}), and if it vanishes at $\\tau_1$.\nFor any horizontal vector field $Y$ along $\\gamma$ we denote by\n$\\Jac(Y)$ the expression on the left-hand\nside of Equation~(\\ref{jaceqn}).\n\\end{definition}\n\nIn fact, there is a similar result even for $\\tau_1=0$.","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[<span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"${\\mathcal L}$\">${\\mathcal L}$</span>-Jacobi field]<span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6c2d6a61636f62692d6669656c64\"></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_ComparisonGeometry%23lem%3Al-jacobi-equation\">↗ lem:l-jacobi-equation</a> <p></p>A field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$Y(\\tau )$\">$Y(\\tau )$</span> along an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"${\\mathcal L}$\">${\\mathcal L}$</span>-geodesic is called an <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"${\\mathcal L}$\">${\\mathcal L}$</span>-Jacobi field if it satisfies the <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"${\\mathcal L}$\">${\\mathcal L}$</span>-Jacobi equation, Equation (<a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_ComparisonGeometry%23jaceqn\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry#jaceqn\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6a616365716e\">jaceqn</a>), and if it vanishes at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tau _1$\">$\\tau _1$</span>. For any horizontal vector field <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$Y$\">$Y$</span> along <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma $\">$\\gamma $</span> we denote by <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\Jac (Y)$\">$\\Jac (Y)$</span> the expression on the left-hand side of Equation (<a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh06_ComparisonGeometry%23jaceqn\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry#jaceqn\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6a616365716e\">jaceqn</a>).  <p></p>In fact, there is a similar result even for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tau _1=0$\">$\\tau _1=0$</span>.","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry#jaceqn","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry#lem:l-jacobi-field-initial-limit","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry#lem:l-jacobi-equation","title":"lem:l-jacobi-equation","label":"lem:l-jacobi-equation"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch06_ComparisonGeometry#lem:l-jacobi-field-initial-limit","title":"lem:l-jacobi-field-initial-limit","label":"lem:l-jacobi-field-initial-lim